course: dictionary
lesson: 13501
title: Words that mean it does not matter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound hard, but they hide a simple idea. Immaterial means not important, or not relevant to what is being talked about. «Whether the cake is chocolate or vanilla is immaterial, because everyone is coming to the party anyway.» The clue is that the flavour does not change anything: it does not matter here.
explain: Ask yourself: would this change the answer? If not, the detail is immaterial. In a maths problem, «Sam has 5 apples, and his shoes are blue.» The shoes are immaterial: you do not need them to answer the question.
explain: Immaterial can also be a formal word. It means not made of matter, with no physical body, like a spirit. You will meet this meaning in stories and books about ideas or religion. The words around it will tell you which meaning is used.
fact: Immaterial means not important or not relevant to what is being talked about.
fact: «That's immaterial» means «that doesn't matter here».
fact: In maths, some numbers are immaterial: they are given, but you don't need them to solve the problem.
fact: Formal meaning: immaterial means not made of matter, with no physical body, like a spirit or the soul.
exercise: «Whether we walk or take the bus is immaterial, as long as we get there.» What does immaterial mean here? | Very loud | Very heavy | *Not important | Made of metal
exercise: A maths problem says, «Sam has 5 apples, and his shoes are blue.» Which detail is immaterial? | *The shoes being blue | The 5 apples | Sam's name
exercise: Which word means the same as immaterial in the everyday sense? | Solid | *Irrelevant | Important | Heavy
test: «The judge said the colour of the car was immaterial to the case.» What does immaterial mean? | Painted red | Very expensive | *Not important to the case
test: «The ghost was immaterial, with no body at all.» Which meaning fits? | Very cheap | Not important | Hard to see in the dark | *Not made of matter, with no physical body
exam: «Whether it rains or not is immaterial to our plans, because we are going indoors.» What is the best meaning of immaterial? | Wet and cold | Solid and heavy | Very happy | *Not important to the plans
